{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is scored exactly once with the built-in `normal_id_glm` sampling statement after all parameters have received built-in priors. Other data variables (`N`, `J`, `county`, and `x`) are context inputs only.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=1> J; // number of counties
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
transformed data {
  matrix[N, 1] cov = [x']';
}
parameters {
  vector[1] beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  real mu_a;
  vector<offset=mu_a, multiplier=sigma_a>[J] a;
}
model {
  beta ~ std_normal();
  mu_a ~ std_normal();
  sigma_a ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  sigma_y ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);

  a ~ normal(mu_a, sigma_a);
  y ~ normal_id_glm(cov, a[county], beta, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{
  "J": 4,
  "N": 2,
  "county": [
    1,
    1
  ],
  "x": [
    6.68836138460955,
    4.766030421866344
  ],
  "y": [
    2.0,
    2.0
  ]
}","protected_variables":["y"]}
